    "reason": "The only evidence is a changelog title [ev-41df2d850c70]: Argo CD now gives better error messages when a StatefulSet update hits an immutable field. So the only environments that see a difference are those where a sync tries to change an immutable StatefulSet field. Whether that happens depends on the live objects compared with the desired manifests at sync time, and no setting, flag or values key can show it in advance. That makes an undecidable leaf with reason runtime-behavior-gap a fair fit, rather than a missing-configuration problem.",
